cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository in research, teaching, or applied work, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "ArchDistribution: A QGIS plugin for reconciling and mapping archaeological spatial records"
authors:
  - family-names: Hwang
    given-names: Jinseo
    affiliation: "Nuri Institute for Archaeology, Republic of Korea"
repository-code: "https://github.com/lzpxilfe/ArchDistribution"
url: "https://github.com/lzpxilfe/ArchDistribution"
version: 1.0.5
license: GPL-2.0-or-later
abstract: >
  A QGIS plugin for reproducible, human-in-the-loop production of
  archaeological distribution maps. It separates archaeological site
  identity, investigation events, geometry grouping, and displayed numbering
  while preserving source records and review evidence.
keywords:
  - archaeology
  - digital archaeology
  - cultural heritage
  - research software
  - gis
  - spatial analysis
  - record linkage
